evidence.code_context:
The vulnerable code is in the persistent_load method of the Deserializer class which extends pickle.Unpickler:

class Deserializer(pickle.Unpickler):
    def persistent_load(self, id_):
        m = our_ids.match(str(id_))
        if not m:
            return None
        else:
            type_, args = m.group(1, 2)
            if type_ == 'attribute':
                key, clsarg = args.split(':')
                cls = pickle.loads(b64decode(clsarg))  # Line 150
                return getattr(cls, key)
            elif type_ == 'mapper':
                cls = pickle.loads(b64decode(args))  # Line 153
                return class_mapper(cls)
            elif type_ == 'mapper_selectable':
                cls = pickle.loads(b64decode(args))  # Line 156 - VULNERABLE
                return class_mapper(cls).__clause_element__()
            elif type_ == 'mapperprop':
                mapper, keyname = args.split(':')
                cls = pickle.loads(b64decode(mapper))  # Line 160
                return class_mapper(cls).attrs[keyname]

The loads() function at line 179 accepts untrusted data and creates a Deserializer that deserializes it, triggering these unsafe pickle.loads() calls.

